			"Message": "build(deps): bump astro from 6.4.5 to 6.4.6\n\nBumps [astro](https://github.com/withastro/astro/tree/HEAD/packages/astro) from 6.4.5 to 6.4.6.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/withastro/astro/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/astro/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/withastro/astro/commits/astro@6.4.6/packages/astro)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: astro\n  dependency-version: 6.4.6\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "1f77d85548db6b86d93fa0de5c1c117be6fa822e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:19:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Consolidate Vite external config into single function\n\nRollup's `external` option accepts either an array or a function, but a mixed array (strings + function) causes the function to be silently ignored. Replace the spread of `External` string prefixes with inline prefix checks inside a single function to ensure all external rules are evaluated.\n\nThe bundled-workbench profile logic is preserved: when `BundledActive` is true, Rollup walks `vs/**` imports for CSS extraction and chunk deduplication, while Wind compiled output and `vscode` remain external. All VSCode internal import patterns (`/vs/`, `/base/common/`, `/platform/`, `/workbench/`, `@codeeditorland/output/Target/Microsoft/VSCode/vs/**`) are now handled in the unified function with both forward and backslash path variants.",
			"SHA": "910ab409e6c23e185e5e8625fb5efccdd1500db9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T14:46:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				8
			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Handle VSCode internal imports in Wind output and update config\n\nAdd build-time handling for VSCode internal relative imports that are transitively included through Wind's compiled output. These imports (e.g., ../../../base/common/buffer.js) resolve at runtime but cause Rollup build errors. Added a Vite plugin to stub these imports as external virtual modules during the build to prevent resolution failures.\n\nAlso update import statements and external configuration to properly handle Wind's compiled output tree. Format JSON files for consistency.",
			"SHA": "4ba7a30292ea7c6549cf0eabbbadb5e95016ab9c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T13:06:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Add @vite-ignore to Wind dynamic imports and format import statements\n\nAdd `/* @vite-ignore */` comments to dynamic imports from `@codeeditorland/wind` packages in Electron entry points and extension change subscriber. This prevents Vite from attempting to bundle these runtime-loaded modules during build.\n\nAlso reformat multiline import statements for consistency across Electron bootstrap, bundled entry, and extension change subscriber files.",
			"SHA": "6f05fb2a3613f4bb999293f936623b9c6dc6dc2d"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1782748806492
